<title>ITALY: Banco Sicilia returns to profit after three years.</title>
<headline>Banco Sicilia returns to profit after three years.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit (loss)	11.5    vs    (273.9)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	272.7    vs     212.1</p>
<p>    Total deposits     40,519	vs  37,940</p>
<p>    Client loans	 25,220	vs  25,834</p>
<p>    Client deposits    29,425	vs  28,141</p>
<p>    Net worth	     1,368	vs     948</p>
<p>Note - Banco di Sicilia is the second largest state-owned bank in southern Italy.</p>
<p>The bank has made a loss for the three years prior to 1996 and its said profitibility was mainly due to substantial increase in income from financial transactions and tight cost control. -- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
